## 1. What This Is

The CAM Lease Analyzer is a web application that reduces landlord legal risk by structurally surfacing material deviations in commercial tenant leases while suppressing cosmetic noise.

It compares tenant leases against a landlord's standard template across 18 provisions, using multiple independent AI evaluators with rule-based governance to determine which differences are substantive and which are benign. The system catches what matters and stays quiet about what doesn't.

It's the first product application of a broader patent-pending framework called the Constrained Assertion Method (CAM), which governs when AI systems should assert conclusions, qualify them, or abstain entirely.

**The core problem it solves:** A landlord's attorney receives a stack of tenant leases. Each should match the standard template, but tenants' attorneys make changes — some obvious, some subtle. Manually comparing 30+ page documents across 18 legal provisions is slow, error-prone, and expensive. The system does this in ~4 minutes per lease at ~$0.30-0.50 per lease, with 96.4% precision and 100% recall. In validation, it caught deviations the test designer missed.

**Target user:** The first user will be a lawyer friend who works with the patent attorney. This is a real professional who will use it on real leases.

