## 3. Lease Analyzer — Product Overview

### What It Does

1. User uploads a standard lease template and one or more tenant leases
2. User selects which provisions to check (18 defaults + custom provisions)
3. System analyzes each tenant lease against the template
4. Results show: which provisions deviate, how, why it matters, what to do
5. User gets an annotated tenant lease (DOCX or PDF with highlights/comments) + synopsis PDF
6. All uploaded documents are deleted after processing

### Key Features

- **Multi-tenant batch processing** — Analyze multiple leases in one job
- **18 default provisions** — Rent, escalation, CAM charges, insurance, subletting, force majeure, etc.
- **Custom provisions** — User can add their own provision descriptions
- **4 AI providers** — Google (Gemini), Anthropic (Claude), OpenAI (GPT-5.2), xAI (Grok)
- **Multi-stage pipeline** — Extraction → Rules → Evaluation → Challenge → Severity → Disposition
- **Annotated output documents** — DOCX callout blocks or PDF highlight annotations
- **Synopsis PDF** — Combined findings across all tenants with full clause text
- **Email notifications** — With attached synopsis and annotated documents
- **Document comparison view** — Full-document or side-by-side comparison with tenant-led or reference-led ordering
- **Feedback mechanism** — User can agree/disagree/mark unsure on each finding
- **Access code gate** — Controls demo access
- **Live deployment** — Railway-hosted demo at `https://cam-production-5cc0.up.railway.app/`
- **24-hour result expiry** — Auto-deletion controlled by `JOB_EXPIRY_MINUTES=1440`

