## 16. Validation Results

### Test Suite

- Standard retail lease template (5,301 words, Meridian Town Center)
- 10 tenant variations: T-01 (clean/identical) through T-10 (sophisticated counsel)
- 27 ground-truth deviations including definition cascades, quantitative changes, omissions
- Manually verified per-provision truth JSON for each tenant

### Performance (test_004b — 10 tenants × 18 provisions = 180 checks)

| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| **Precision** | 96.4% (27/28 flagged are real deviations) |
| **Recall** | 100% (all 27 real deviations caught — zero misses) |
| **False positives** | 1 (T-04 LP-05, borderline cascade) |
| **False negatives** | 0 |
| **Cost per tenant** | ~$0.30-0.50 |
| **Time per tenant** | ~4 minutes |

### Governance Quality — Calibration by Disposition Type

This is CAM's core value proposition: the system's confidence levels are meaningful, not just its accuracy.

| Disposition Path | Count (180 checks) | Accuracy | What It Shows |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Unanimous CONFORMS + no rules** (triage pass) | ~122 | 100% | When all evaluators agree and no rules fire, the system is always right. Zero false negatives in this category. |
| **Challenged DEVIATES** (full pipeline) | 27 | 96.4% | Deviations that survived adversarial challenge. One borderline FP (T-04 LP-05). |
| **Rule-only flags** (rules fired, evaluators agreed CONFORMS) | ~31 | 100% | Rules flagged provisions for review that evaluators correctly cleared. No missed deviations in this path. |

This proves the triage gate is epistemically meaningful — the system's certainty levels correspond to actual correctness rates.

### Triage as Epistemic Compression

The triage gate is quietly the system's most commercially interesting feature. It works by suppressing unnecessary cost and review noise while preserving safety:

- **~30% of provisions skip challenge and severity** (unanimous CONFORMS + no rules)
- **Those skipped provisions had 100% correctness in validation**
- **Zero false negatives escaped the triage gate**

This means the system's "fast path" is as reliable as its "deep path" for clean provisions, while the deep path catches real deviations with 96.4% precision. Enterprise buyers care about this: it proves the system knows when to spend compute and when not to.

### Notable Discoveries

- System caught deviations the test designer missed (T-02 LP-17 "prevailing party" → "substantially prevails"; T-07 LP-05 Force Majeure cascade)
- Definition cascades required a dedicated micro-stage — the general challenger couldn't handle both directions
- Provider selection functions as an "epistemic posture dial" — doesn't affect core accuracy (demonstrated in ContractNLI Phase 3)

